{
  "id": "social-relations-model",
  "term": "social relations model",
  "definition": "The social relations model is a way of studying interdependence in families or other groups by breaking each pairwise interaction score into shared group influence, each person’s general tendency as actor and as partner, and what is unique to that specific relationship. It is used in family assessment to help describe how a particular family functions and how its interaction patterns compare with a reference sample.",
